### App Initialization and Lifecycle

The `AppLayout.tsx` component is the root wrapper of the Rocket.Chat client application. It performs global UI and session initialization, including:

- Adding global body CSS classes for theming.
- Setting up OAuth integration hooks for supported providers (GitHub, GitLab, Apple, Nextcloud, WordPress, etc.).
- Initializing analytics tracking and Google Tag Manager.
- Managing notification permissions.
- Handling auto-update notifications for app deployments.
- Configuring UI behavior features (e.g., emoji support, hotkeys, iframe messaging).
- Reactively subscribing to layout state changes exposed by the `appLayout` store.

```tsx
// Snippet from AppLayout.tsx initialization
useEffect(() => {
	document.body.classList.add('color-primary-font-color', 'rcx-content--main');
	return () => {
		document.body.classList.remove('color-primary-font-color', 'rcx-content--main');
	};
}, []);

useIframeLoginListener();
useMessageLinkClicks();
useGoogleTagManager();
useAnalytics();
useEscapeKeyStroke();
useKeyboardShortcutsHotkey();
useAnalyticsEventTracking();
useLoadRoomForAllowedAnonymousRead();
useNotificationPermission();
useEmojiOne();
// [...many custom OAuth and UI hooks...]

const layout = useSyncExternalStore(appLayout.subscribe, appLayout.getSnapshot);

return (
	<Suspense fallback={<PageLoading />}>
		<DocumentTitleWrapper>{layout}</DocumentTitleWrapper>
	</Suspense>
);
```

